# @NAME@ for Pokitto

Generated by `gbrecomp --target pokitto`. Same runtime and generated code as
the Gamebuino META build (`--target meta`); the Pokitto drivers are in
`src/pokitto_*.c`. Workflow, tests and limitations are documented in
`targets/meta/README.md` of the gb-recompiled repository.

```bash
# Firmware: bare metal, only arm-none-eabi-gcc (PATH, or PlatformIO's toolchain)
make                         # build/firmware.bin, flash report below the loader

# Host tools (identical to the META project)
cmake -G Ninja -S host -B host/build && ninja -C host/build
host/build/@NAME@_play --interp --coverage more.cov --record-input more.input
host/build/@NAME@_host --frames 3000 --input more.input
```

Copy `build/firmware.bin` to the SD card as `@NAME@.bin`, with the game's
`.SAV`, `.STA` and streamed `.GB` files next to it when the build uses them.

Pokitto controls: D-pad, A, B; C tap = Start; C + B = Select; C held half a
second opens the option menu (save states, volume, palette, frame skip,
48/72 MHz, back to the loader). C held at power-on starts the Pokitto
loader. The picture is the Game Boy's 160x144, unscaled, in the middle of
the 220x176 screen.
